The three finished checks were healthy, and the document is clearly needed to answer. I submitted four more checks; the campaign now waits for them.

## Done
- **Three checks finished cleanly.** Each ran once with no errors and every row was scored by the judge:
  - "closed-book" (the uncompressed model gets only the question, no document): 1,407 questions;
  - uncompressed text at a 512-token answer limit: 300 rows;
  - the first mixed run (some pages given as text, others as images): 300 rows.
- **The 512-token answer limit stays.** Only 8 of 300 uncompressed text answers (2.7%) hit it, under the 5% bar. I now count this with the real tokenizer instead of by characters. The character count was wrong both ways: 8.3% vs 11.0% real at 256 tokens, and 6.3% vs 2.7% real at 512. The campaign rules and known-issues file now require the tokenizer count.
- **The answers come from the document, not from the model's memory.** This is a first read on 300 trial rows; the full uncompressed runs will decide it. The bar is +20 points over closed-book, and every length passes with a wide margin:

| set | lengths | questions per length | uncompressed with the document (judge ↑) | closed-book (judge ↑) | difference (points ↑) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| pages | 10 / 20 / 40 pages | 100 | .71 / .71 / .73 | .19 | +52 / +52 / +54 |
| text | ~4k / 8k / 16k / 32k tokens | 75 | .587 / .587 / .587 / .573 | .253 | +33 / +33 / +33 / +32 |
| mixed | 10 / 20 / 40 items | 100 | .63 / .66 / .67 | .19 | +44 / +47 / +48 |

- **The uncompressed model does not get worse as text gets longer**, from ~4k to ~32k tokens. The inputs really differ by length: only 5 of 75 questions get the same answer at every length.
- I fixed the claim the read-only verifier had flagged. The count of long-document rows beyond anything seen in training is now saved in `expQ/longdoc/audit_191516/out_of_range.json`.
- I also wrote a small pairing script, `scripts/longdoc/closedbook_pair.py`, and updated `docs/longdoc_diagnosis.md` and `STATE.md`.

## Running now (4 new submissions, the per-wake maximum)
- **Planted-fact checks, uncompressed, for text, pages and mixed:** a fact is placed at 10%, 50% or 90% of the way through a real document. A length where the model finds fewer than 90% of them is dropped from the set.
- **The first compressed-model run on mixed documents (300 rows):** it measures the last missing run time needed for the cost estimate.

## Next
- Read the four results.
- Launch the second-seed runs still missing for the length test: 20 pages and 40 text passages.
- Then send you one question with the measured cost of the full long-document runs. My rough estimate is about 75 GPU-hours, against about 30 left in the budget. The campaign rules forbid trimming the runs to fit, so this goes to you.

Nothing needed from you now. The campaign wakes again when the four jobs finish, or in 6 hours at most.
